# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: alfe-cad-source-loader-evaluates-block-comments - documentation text is executed as AutoLISP
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: cad-runtime
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-alfe-cad-source-loader-evaluates-block-comments
#+DATE: 2026-10-08

* Observed

SCHMS CI job 529707, =test-cad-activex:autocad:windows=, uses ALFE
2.2.227 and fails while loading the test harness, before any test runs:

https://fabrik.sncf.fr/gitlab/dmoe-pop/epure/es/schms/-/jobs/529707

#+begin_example
while loading autolisp-test/vlisp-project.lsp
(form starting at line 87) at line 87, column 1:
no function definition: SYMBOLE
#+end_example

The nested load chain is =test-cad-activex.lsp= ->
=tests/test-runner-commun.lsp= -> =autolisp-test/test-runner.lsp= ->
=autolisp-test/vlisp-project.lsp=. The last file contains:

#+begin_src lisp
;| @Global
  Nom d'une clé de propriété (symbole ou autre valeur), en majuscules.
  @Param key A: clé lue dans la liste de propriétés
  @Returns string: par exemple ":OWN-LIST"
|;
(defun vlisp-project--key-name (key)
  (strcase
    (if (= (type key) 'SYM)
      (vl-symbol-name key)
      (vl-princ-to-string key))))
#+end_src

=SYMBOLE= is prose inside a valid block comment, not a missing application
function. The loader is treating =(symbole ou autre valeur)= as code.
This documentation format is required by SCHMS and used by outils-autolisp.

* Minimal regression case to run

Save the following as =block-comment-repro.lsp= and load it through the
CAD backend, for example =alfe -norc --autocad -l block-comment-repro.lsp=:

#+begin_src lisp
;| @Global
  Description (symbole ou autre valeur).
|;
(setq block-comment-repro-ok T)
(princ "BLOCK-COMMENT-OK")
(princ)
#+end_src

Expected: the comment is ignored, the assignment executes and stdout
contains =BLOCK-COMMENT-OK=. There must be no evaluation of =SYMBOLE=.
This reduced case has not yet been run; the CI failure above is observed.

* Cause identified by source inspection

In =autolisp-front-end/source/runtime/autolisp-bootstrap.lsp=,
=autolisp-source-scan-text=, =autolisp-source-leading-symbols=,
=autolisp-source-trim-leading-junk= and
=autolisp-source-first-form-end= only track line comments. A semicolon
starts a comment, and a newline ends it. They do not recognise the
=;|= / =|;= block-comment delimiters.

Consequently the opening documentation line is discarded as a line
comment, while subsequent prose, including its parentheses, is scanned
as executable forms. Fix the shared lexical handling rather than
removing documentation or defining a dummy SYMBOLE function.

* Acceptance criteria

- All CAD source scanning, trimming and form splitting agree on block
  comments and preserve state across lines until =|;=.
- Comment contents are never read or evaluated, including parentheses,
  quotes and semicolons inside the block.
- Delimiters inside string literals remain literal text; ordinary line
  comments retain their semantics.
- Forms before and after a block comment, including on the same line,
  are each executed exactly once. Source locations remain accurate.
- Add regression coverage in =autolisp-front-end/tests/file-protocol-tests.lisp=
  using the hosted protocol harness; verify AutoCAD and BricsCAD when available.
- Loading =autolisp-test/vlisp-project.lsp= and the SCHMS ActiveX entry
  point proceeds beyond the documentation block on AutoCAD.
